  texts:
  - TRANSLATION
  - ELEVATION
  - ROTATION
  - FUSION & PARTITION
  - STORM & FINAL CHOICE
  - "Ending C  \u2022  Open Archive"
  - Vela climbs the observation fence as an old radio signal comes back. It is not the SIM system voice but a recording of residents who once planted a message in the silent room.
  - Danu never returned to the control tower, but his piano score played across every district speaker before the storm subsided.
  - 'You stand as Rect at the edge of the pier: the simulation system slowly opens, giving the city room to remember who it is.'
  - 'With Partition [1], the energy core is split: half closes the emergency floodgate, half powers the community transmitter tower.'
  - The District Goes on Air
  - 'Community Transmitter: partition CORE-01 with [1] or activate the transmitter plate in the center.'
  - The final-choice socket requires CORE-01.
  - "Ending B  \u2022  Eternal Vault"
  - Outside the archive walls, waves still strike the old foundation. Several piers must be abandoned while residents move to higher ground.
  - Inside the vault, though, the warm yellow light stays on. Every fragment you collected is laid out neatly so the next generation still knows this city's song.
  - The system stops counting score; all that remains is a silent keeper named Rect.
  - The energy core is placed in the West Archive Vault. Every photo, letter, and recording from the district is perfectly protected from storm corrosion.
  - Memories Kept Behind Glass
  - 'Final Choice: Carry CORE-01 East (Levee), North (Transmitter + Partition [1]), or West (Vault)'
  - "Ending A  \u2022  Levee Closed"
  - The seawater recedes, leaving a dry pier and an intact market street. Mira helps residents relight the apartment block.
  - In the archive building, frozen silent, the SIM display shows a green status. No names remain in the history list, only tidy building coordinates.
  - Rect gazes at the sea from behind the levee, holding a single piano note whose owner is unknown.
  - All core power is routed to the North Levee. The storm surge is held outside the wall, but the entire underground memory bank floods with it.
  - City Saved, Memory Buried
  - If you can still hear this recording, Rect... Tepi City isn't truly gone yet.
  - We live in this quiet room with the voices that were left behind.
  - Voices Behind the Glass
  - Back then, the smell of bread always reached the corner before the sun came up.
  - Now all that's left are containment boxes and light barriers.
  - Morning Bread Stall
  - If the archive bridge rises again someday, it means someone refuses to forget this city.
  - The bridge needs two weights at once. Don't leave either one behind.
  - Shift Closing Letter
  - When the power flickered, these stairs were the only way out for the residents.
  - In Flexible Mode you can jump and pull weights from a distance.
  - Second-Floor Clothesline
  - From this roof we can see the entire north dyke before the water rises.
  - Keep the elevation path intact, Nara. The archive is on the other side.
  - Nara's Transmitter Antenna
  - All the old archive doors only lock when the symbol on their side faces the right direction.
  - The wrong angle will only bounce the core out.
  - Archive Chamber Twist Lock
  - Danu always said music can't be measured by a grid. He put it in an unindexed corner of the room.
  - If the system starts freezing the residents' memories, this tone will unlock them again.
  - Untitled Score
  - "Two objects combined with Fusion don't have to be the same kind \u2014 a cube and a prism still merge into a new composite."
  - 'FUSION [2] active: combine two objects of different shape and mass into one composite core.'
  - Law of Conservation of Space
  - Storing all the data in one big lump is dangerous. Split it so it can fill both guardians at once.
  - 'PARTITION [1] active: split one heavy object into two balanced parts.'
  - Controlled Fragments
  - When Partition and Fusion are used alternately, no mass is wasted.
  - The storm at the outer levee is starting to be heard. Get ready to head to the main city.
  - Final Laboratory Notes
  - Stormwater has reached the outer side of the control room. Soon all paths lead to the final decision chamber.
  - Remember, you still have full control to split or join whatever remains.
  - North Levee Wave
  - We won't force you to choose, Rect.
  - Save the levee, lock the archive, or split its energy so our voices survive too.
  - Voices of Tepi City Residents
  - 'All main mechanics active in this room: Translation, Elevation, Rotation, Partition [1]/[3], and Hybrid Fusion [2].'
  - Use [TAB] for Flexible Mode, [F] Telekinesis, [R] Rotation, [1] Partition, [3] Cut Direction, and [2] Fusion.
  - POLYMULATOR Demo Archive
  - Auto (Rect Facing)
  - Front | Back Axis (Z)
  - Top | Bottom Axis (Y)
  - Left | Right Axis (X)
  - AUTOMATIC
  - FRONT | BACK
  - TOP | BOTTOM
  - LEFT | RIGHT
  - 'Bring held {0} near another object to begin Fusion [2]'
  - '{0} cannot be fused'
  - '{0} ({1}): {2} + {3}'
  - '{0} can only be fused with another CORE-01 piece nearby'
  - CORE-01 restored intact through Fusion!
  - Maximum fusion limit ({0} parts) reached
  - 'Lift an object first [E], then move it near another object to Fuse [2]'
  - '{0} + {1}'
  - TWIN-BLOCK
  - TWIN-PILLAR
  - ORB-SOCKET
  - ORB-PEDESTAL
  - MODULAR-ASSEMBLY
  - MODULAR-TOWER
  - AXLE-MODULE
  - CYLINDER-TURRET
  - TWIN-TURBINE
  - TOWER-PISTON
  - ORB-PISTON
  - ORB-BEACON
  - ORB-BARBELL
  - TWIN-CORE
  - Block
  - Assembly
  - Cylinder
  - Sphere
  - BACK
  - FRONT
  - LEFT
  - RIGHT
  - TOP
  - 'Side {0} is blocked. Choose another side [WASD / Q / 3]'
  - Fusion stage cancelled
  - "CHAPTER 1  \u2022  TRANSLATION"
  - Main key installed. The door to the Market District is open.
  - Behind the light on this chamber's walls, shadows of the old streets begin to appear.
  - TEST CHAMBER 01
  - Voices Behind the Glass
  - Move Rect with WASD or the arrow keys toward the yellow cube CORE-01.
  - Press [E] to lift CORE-01, carry it to the round socket ANCHOR-01 to the north, then press [E] or [Q] to put it down.
  - "The pink crystal on the left side is optional \u2014 touch it to hear a story fragment."
  - Simulation session starting. Unit Rect is back online in Test Chamber 01.
  - A yellow core glows in the middle of the floor. Someone left it right on your path.
  - Build in an Empty Chamber
  - "CHAPTER 1  \u2022  TRANSLATION"
  - Good, the path is open again. Let's keep going toward the archive building.
  - OLD MARKET STREET
  - Morning Bread Stall
  - Lift the BEBAN-PASAR block with [E], then place it on the PAD-PASAR floor plate on the left.
  - When the plate turns green and the red barrier disappears, bring CORE-01 to ANCHOR-01 to the north.
  - 'Tip: press [Left Click] while holding a block if you want to push it forward.'
  - The red gate ahead is locked by the weight plate on the left floor.
  - Find a weight block around the hallway to turn off the barrier.
  - Market Street
  - "CHAPTER 1  \u2022  TRANSLATION"
  - Translation Sector complete. Access to the apartment building's elevation level is open.
  - ARCHIVE GATE
  - Shift Closing Letter
  - Place BEBAN-BARAT on PAD-BARAT and BEBAN-TIMUR on PAD-TIMUR.
  - If both plates are green, the bridge stairs in the middle will extend until they reach the upper deck.
  - Carry CORE-01 up along the bridge stairs to ANCHOR-01.
  - The stairs to the archive deck are broken in the middle.
  - Activate both floor plates so the energy bridge connects fully.
  - East Archive Gate
  - "CHAPTER 2  \u2022  ELEVATION"
  - Slowly, this old building is starting to respond to our steps again.
  - MATAHARI APARTMENTS // L1
  - Second-Floor Clothesline
  - Press [TAB] to switch movement mode to Flexible Mode (purple).
  - Lift BEBAN-UNGU via the left balcony stairs, or aim at BEBAN-UNGU and press [F] to lift it with telekinesis onto PAD-BALKON.
  - Once the right bridge is active, bring CORE-01 up to the Anchor Deck.
  - The bridge trigger plate is on the left balcony!
  - Press [TAB] to switch to Flexible Mode so Rect can jump and use [F] telekinesis.
