  - "CHAPTER 4  \u2022  FUSION & PARTITION"
  - One object becomes two keys. A fair split saves this path.
  - PARTITION CHAMBER // 02
  - Controlled Fragments
  - 'Approach or hold the large MONOLIT block (2.4 t): the laser plane line shows the cut direction in real-time.'
  - Use [3] to change the cut axis (Auto / X / Z / Y), then press [1] to split MONOLIT into MONOLIT-A & -B (1.2 t x 2).
  - Place each fragment on PAD-KIRI and PAD-KANAN, then bring CORE-01 up the bridge.
  - There is only one MONOLIT block weighing 2.4 t. The orange laser plane shows where the pieces will fall.
  - By default the cut direction follows Rect's facing; press [3] to rotate the cutting plane (Left|Right, Front|Back, Top|Bottom), then [1] PARTITION.
  - One Split into Two
  - "CHAPTER 4  \u2022  FUSION & PARTITION"
